Web API interface
===================

The web app exposes an HTTP interface that downstream clients integrate
against: ``GET /version`` returns the project version as plain text and
``GET /info`` returns a JSON object with the version and runtime environment,
both served by the {{ "FastAPI" if web_framework == "fastapi" else "Litestar" }}
application at ``{{github_repo_name}}.web.app:app``.

The `OpenAPI <https://www.openapis.org/>`_ specification below is the
machine-readable contract for that interface — the routes, response schemas,
and status codes (including the ``503`` returned when the package metadata is
unavailable). It is generated on every docs build directly from the live
``app`` object, so it stays in lockstep with the code.

.. literalinclude:: _generated/openapi.yaml
   :language: yaml
   :caption: openapi.yaml

.. note::

   To regenerate the schema locally outside a docs build:

   .. code-block:: console

{%- if web_framework == "litestar" %}

      $ uv run --group docs litestar --app {{github_repo_name}}.web.app:app \
          schema openapi --output docs/_generated/openapi.yaml
{%- else %}

      $ uv run --group docs sphinx-build -b html docs docs/_build/html

   (FastAPI has no first-party file exporter; ``docs/conf.py`` dumps
   ``app.openapi()`` to ``docs/_generated/openapi.{json,yaml}`` as part of the
   Sphinx build.)
{%- endif %}
